WEBVTT

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:35.120
The immense castle is situated in Ranshuu, also known as the city of water.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.370
Canals and moats run across the city,

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:42.950
and if you look down from the sky,
the castle appears to float on the water.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.370
For this reason, the castle is called
"Kokai Castle," the castle of lake and sea.

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:53.460
So, what does the letter from our youngest brother say?

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:58.430
It says he feels as if his world has turned upside down.

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:04.470
After living for eighteen years, he has finally met soul friend number one and number two.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.810
Ryuuren seems to be over the moon.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.900
Now if only Shuuei would come home once in a while.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.550
Gyokuka and I are both waiting for him.

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:19.200
These triplets are the older brothers of Ran Shuuei and Ran Ryuuren

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.330
and are the heads of the distinguished Ran family.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.530
Then make him come home.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:28.580
That's an idea. That Emperor's not worthy of Shuuei.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:34.020
Anyway, it's about time he started suffering for some absurd reason,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.480
like he's not truly loyal to the Emperor.

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:39.340
Hey Setsuna, let's just do it.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:45.220
Setsuna, you never intended to leave Shuuei with the Emperor forever, did you?

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:51.600
You're right. It's about time Shuuei ends this "fun studying" and comes home.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:02.650
In the meantime, an Imperial Court Conference was being held in the capital of Kiyou.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.740
I wish to make a proposal.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:09.410
What could that be?

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:18.010
I propose to dismiss all officials who currently hold the rank of joukan.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:28.280
I-I must say something.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:43.070
Ouki-dono has a point.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.970
Why doesn't he help me out, that blasted old man?!

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.320
Is he sleeping with his eyes open?

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:49.580
Do what you're paid for!

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:52.500
Hmph, you're still wet behind the ears.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.130
That's what you get for sitting around daydreaming.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:02.930
However, not all joukan are worthless, to be sure.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.420
Let's set a time frame,

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:08.950
during which we will assess the candidates and keep those who prove themselves worthy.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.810
Of course.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:18.690
We should single out the joukan who are
particularly incompetent and dismiss them.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:21.400
Let's give them a month.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:26.790
Those who fail to deliver any results in that time will be dealt with.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:27.950
Is that agreeable?

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.980
All right.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.960
One more thing.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:41.340
In order to stabilize the prices of tea, iron, and salt, the most important products of this country,

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:45.510
I propose to create a specific official rank for this task.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:47.760
Yes, that...

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:49.010
That matter will be deferred until next time,

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:50.510
so please bear with us.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:54.520
The measure will be considered at another conference, I assure you.

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:02.730
I'm sorry.

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:05.740
All because I was daydreaming...

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:10.120
You should daydream now and then.
Otherwise, you'll become exhausted.

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:15.710
I must try harder.

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:20.060
There's no need for the Emperor to be perfect, and it's impossible anyway.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:23.550
We vassals are here to compensate for that.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:30.800
But, if one of us advises Your Highness, then please listen carefully.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:35.820
Whether the advice comes from an official or a child playing in the street, treat it the same way.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:45.400
Take only half of the honeyed words seriously,
and take the harsh words as the voice of our people.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:48.320
That's all I ask of you.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:54.330
Yuushun-dono, you only speak honeyed words to me, I think.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:58.120
Then please only take half of my words seriously.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:01.340
That way I won't ever get truly angry at you.

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:02.440
What?

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:04.840
Right...

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:10.440
But really, I think Your Highness works best when you're just a little slow.

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:14.350
That way, your opponents will underestimate you, and we might be able to take them off guard.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:19.100
Are you talking about official Ou's
proposal about tea, iron, and salt?

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:21.570
I thought that was a fair point.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:27.320
Then when you have time, think about why I opposed the idea.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.740
Okay...

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:33.870
I was planning on reorganizing the officials anyway, so that was fine.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:39.410
However, I'm concerned about Shuurei-dono.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:45.050
Shuurei should be able to fight her way through this like she did in Sashuu, right?

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.690
Yes.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.010
I certainly hope so.

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:57.020
Clearing out the joukan?!

00:06:57.430 --> 00:07:00.370
It's a good thing Yuushun was there.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:03.880
He closed the grave that you and that snot-nosed Emperor foolishly dug for Shuurei.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:04.820
But!

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:07.150
Making Shuurei a joukan was the best way

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:10.700
to shut the mouth of those old foxes in the Imperial Court... back then!

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:12.290
You're too optimistic!

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:16.660
You don't think ahead, and that's why those old foxes can trip you up.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:22.250
If Shuurei can't accomplish this task,

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:26.330
then you and I will end up having to deliver her dismissal notice.

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:28.880
Thanks to that idiot Emperor.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.890
You'll work in the Civil Service Ministry for the time being.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:39.110
Don't expect that you'll be able to fool around with your snot-nosed Emperor.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:40.110
Understood?

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:41.890
Yes.

00:07:57.690 --> 00:07:59.900
The Section of Government Inspection seems to be busy.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:03.960
Kouki, you work too hard.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:07.840
Anjuu, to my eyes, you don't seem to work at all.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:14.090
The plan to wipe out the joukan... is going ahead, apparently.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:16.590
We don't need incompetent personnel.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:20.100
So, you're gonna get rid of Shin Suou, too?

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:25.470
I should've sentenced both him and his father to death, as a pointed lesson for others.

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:29.520
I thought that even if he wasn't useful at work,

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:33.110
he could at least be useful as an official.

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:36.290
I heard that the mistress of the Kou family took him away.

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:38.370
Apparently, she worked very hard for it.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:42.230
That girl is also useless.

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:45.000
She's easily confused by what's right in front of her.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:49.230
We'll find out whether or not she's completely useless during this matter.

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:52.630
I, as the person in charge of the Section of Government Inspection, will monitor her performance.

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:57.270
Don't bully her too much. After all, she <i>is</i> a girl.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:01.760
Stop joking. She brought this on herself.

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:04.810
I won't tolerate such an excuse.

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.350
I thought you'd say that.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:12.190
Well, I'll be kind to her to balance out your heartlessness.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.320
I can't see.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.790
As part of a reorganization of ranks and personnel,

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:41.570
those joukan listed to the right, who are not currently employed, will be dismissed in a month's time.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:42.930
Tan-tan!

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:45.020
See?

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:46.260
What?

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:49.380
Life's not that easy.

00:09:57.560 --> 00:10:00.780
It's written right there, no mistake.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:03.320
My name and yours.

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:05.360
Why are you taking this so lightly?

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:07.160
Don't you care if you get fired like this?

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:10.460
Whether I like it or not, it's already been decided, hasn't it?

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.370
Listen. We've been given a month.

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:15.430
Normally when you're fired, they ask you to leave at the end of the month.

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:17.690
Yet they've provided this extra time before dismissal.

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:22.400
In addition, the reason is clearly stated as
"the reorganization of ranks and personnel"!

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:26.740
You're saying they're testing us?

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:30.890
That's right, and it singles out the joukan who aren't employed.

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:32.680
It doesn't matter where.

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:37.410
Just keep telling them, "I'm useful!", and find work within a month!

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:39.540
That way they can't fire us!

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:41.910
They're still short of officials, if I remember correctly.

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:45.330
Aren't you taking this too much in stride?

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:48.050
What else could I do if I didn't take it in stride and work hard on it?

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:51.920
You and I can't afford to just hang our heads and walk away from this, can we?!

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:55.060
You're gonna render some distinguished service and save your father, right?

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:58.910
Well, my parents will do something about it when I tell them.

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:03.200
I'm still sleepy because I woke up early.

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:06.000
I'm going home now to write a letter to my father.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.700
Yeah, me too. Let's go.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:14.000
Hey, are you sure?!

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:16.440
You might get fired, you know?

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:19.730
Well, isn't this your fault?

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:22.990
This never happened to us before.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:27.520
It's a nuisance. We're collateral damage because you were removed from office.

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:33.710
I think this notice of dismissal was to be expected!

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:36.130
This workplace isn't normal!

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:40.510
Of course you'll get fired if all you do is get paid for lazing around!

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:43.760
On top of that, taxes pay our wages!

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.260
It's taxpayers' money!

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:48.970
It's money everyone gets for working hard and sweating blood,

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:50.590
which you lot pocket without even working.

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:54.150
It's the taxpayers who are suffering from nuisances, not you!

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:58.710
You've got to fight through it by showing you can work!

00:11:58.710 --> 00:12:01.900
Yes, I agree with you.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.820
Judging from the names on the list,

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:09.960
it's fair to assume you've all been written off and abandoned.

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:11.790
Wh-What do you mean?

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:14.570
Even though you're all joukan,

00:12:14.570 --> 00:12:17.700
I don't see the names of anyone higher than the middle class.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:20.670
I guess the higher ranking officials already cut a deal.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:23.230
Even if you tell your parents about it now,

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:25.490
they probably won't be able to change the situation.

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:29.180
I thought it would work out somehow once I told my parents.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:31.890
Me too. My parents bought this rank for me.

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:34.060
I haven't managed to make any good contacts at the Imperial Court yet.

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:36.710
If I'm kicked out now, I'll be disowned!

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:38.820
You're disappointed, aren't you,

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:40.650
Kou Shuurei?

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:43.700
But, that's how people get by in this place.

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.950
Even so, it's outrageous.

00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:52.790
Maybe, but logical reasoning and fairness
won't get you anywhere in the Imperial Court.

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:59.600
Didn't anyone teach her that?

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:01.470
What is it?

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:04.290
Probably not...

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:10.110
You said that if we do something within a month, we might be appointed to an office, right?

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:12.100
What? Oh, yes.

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:15.630
I... really want to stay.

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:21.110
Umm, don't tell me... you're asking <i>me</i>
to do something about it?

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:24.510
I don't know what to do or how to do it for myself yet!

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:28.780
Umm, I'm also at a critical moment in my career!

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:30.910
Please help!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.540
Please help us!

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:33.980
What?

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:39.470
Shuuei.

00:13:39.910 --> 00:13:41.540
Shuu-ei.

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:43.050
Oh, y-yes.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:44.750
What's wrong?

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:47.570
Did Shusui yell at you again?

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:49.470
H-Has Shusui said something?

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:52.500
She often complains about you to me.

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:55.840
"Don't mistake the Imperial Residence for some kind of brothel."

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:59.520
"Like a mosquito larva, he keeps turning up no matter how often you get rid of him."

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:02.780
I'm... sorry about that.

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:04.070
No problem.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:07.520
I wonder what Kouyuu would say if he heard about it.

00:14:07.520 --> 00:14:10.490
He'd probably tell you off in a loud voice.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:12.990
Don't you think about the circumstances?!

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:17.400
It's too quiet without Kouyuu. It doesn't feel right.

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:18.390
Yeah.

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:21.630
The Civil Service will be busy for the next month. It can't be helped.

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:26.260
Would you miss me if I left you too?

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:30.260
Of course.

00:14:35.050 --> 00:14:38.400
Thank you... Your Highness.

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:42.040
Shuuei, let's eat dumplings!

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:42.770
What?

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:46.290
Yuushun-dono's wife gave some to me.

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:48.780
And let's play a game of go.

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:51.030
Okay...

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:55.800
If you win, you get a bit of a holiday, just a bit.

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:58.680
I'm warning you beforehand, I'm probably not a bad player.

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:00.540
I'm probably a good player.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:02.330
Oh? Well, you said it.

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:10.380
In terms of age, I'm the eldest, followed by Kouyuu, then Your Highness, I suppose.

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:13.690
No, I'm the middle.

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:17.390
From the top: Shuuei, me, then Kouyuu.

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:23.280
Hey, you ate me head first?

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:27.860
I'm going to play hard against you, so I'm provoking you first.

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:30.620
Well then, shall we begin?

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:31.420
Sure.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:34.920
H-Hey, Tan-tan.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:36.480
Yeah?

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:39.490
Am I the only one scared of looking over my shoulder?

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:40.270
Oh.

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:49.400
Just forget about them.

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:54.710
It's not like you're their guardian or supervisor, are you?

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:56.130
I agree.

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:56.850
What?

00:15:57.760 --> 00:15:59.870
Well, umm...

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.480
Allow me to introduce myself.

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:04.980
I'm Riku Seiga.

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:06.980
R-Right...

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:10.330
I don't think you should worry about them.

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:14.910
They're all quite well off at home.

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:19.080
So, do you think you can sort yourself out somehow?

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:25.250
Sure, my supervisor only made me a joukan temporarily because of circumstances at work.

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:27.150
Really?

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:29.240
The problem here is...

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:34.290
You don't have time for them.

00:16:34.290 --> 00:16:40.430
Of course, I'll take care of myself, but if I can do
something for them in passing, then I want to try.

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:44.090
So the rumors I've heard about you are true.

00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:46.690
If you're planning on doing something, I'd be happy to help.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:50.240
No, please don't encourage her, okay?

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:53.570
Would you mind not declining the help he's kindly offered?!

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:57.430
I call it meddling, not helping!

00:16:57.430 --> 00:17:03.120
Don't accept anything that's offered to you for free, just because you're poor.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.830
Especially when you can barely manage your own life!

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:09.840
Why would you voluntarily try to sort out other people's troubles?

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.460
Tan-tan...

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:24.930
Stand up!

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:27.650
This is not your home or playground! It's your workplace!

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:31.690
At the end of the day, whether or not you get fired is up to you!

00:17:31.690 --> 00:17:34.990
If you don't want to be fired, grab a job yourself!

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:36.030
Got it?!

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:38.990
She listens to your words.

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:37.890
Now get moving!

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:42.490
You're better than I thought, Suou-san.

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:47.760
Let's go, Tan-tan.

00:17:56.310 --> 00:17:58.620
Wh-What happened to this room?

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:03.450
This is the room for joukan?

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:11.830
Oh, so you have books at least...

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:13.320
That's...

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:20.660
Th-This is...

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:23.140
A peach-colored book. You've never seen one before?

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:24.390
Of course not!

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:30.280
That's what men are like, you know.

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:35.210
Even your super-handsome family retainer...

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:40.260
is bound to have a book like this hidden under the bed or at the bottom of his closet.

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:42.640
S-Seiran's different!

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:45.320
He wouldn't have that kind of indecent book!

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:48.610
If he had money, he'd give it to me to buy food...

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:49.940
probably...

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:52.730
He definitely has one.

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:54.350
You've got one too, haven't you, Seiga?

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:58.950
Uh, well... I don't have any.

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:00.380
Yeah, right.

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:04.000
It's best to tell the truth sooner rather than later.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:07.620
Because women have stupid fantasies about men, men end up getting dumped—

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:10.330
Who cares about a peach-colored book?!

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:12.420
This is a workplace!

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:14.680
Tidy up! Now!

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:15.860
What?

00:19:15.860 --> 00:19:17.360
I can't be bothered.

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:17.360
No way, impossible.

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:18.420
Do it!

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:28.170
It's finally done.

00:19:28.170 --> 00:19:30.890
I can't believe it's the same room.

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:34.910
How did you manage to hide so many?

00:19:34.910 --> 00:19:36.190
I don't believe this.

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:42.040
You know, the way you react to this is childish and makes you seem like an ordinary girl.

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:43.830
It's rather cute.

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:48.700
Time for a break.

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.330
How about you?

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:54.870
I'm putting this away.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:20:02.470
Basically, she tends not to see men as a threat to her.

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:08.910
Most definitely because of that guy.

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:19.520
Kouyuu-sama...

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:21.400
Is he lost again?

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:23.360
Kouyuu-sama!

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:27.550
Should I walk with you to the Civil Service office?

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:28.670
No...

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:33.000
The current circumstances are my fault. I'm sorry.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:34.300
Why do you say that?

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:37.770
I think the measures being taken are very logical and fair.

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:43.090
Like all other times, I'm just going to do what I can.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:47.090
If you come to the Civil Service, I'll overload you with work.

00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:49.250
Thank you.

00:20:49.690 --> 00:20:53.470
Umm, is Ryuuki feeling down in some strange way again?

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:59.610
I'm mostly at the Civil Service office right now, so I don't know.

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:03.700
Then, he must be missing you, even as we speak.

00:21:06.020 --> 00:21:07.700
I-I lost...

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:13.180
I became quite serious about this game.

00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:16.500
Ah!

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:22.380
Your Highness, please don't eat just the top dumplings because you lost the game.

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.880
You're giving me a sly hint, aren't you?

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:32.590
What is it?

00:21:33.370 --> 00:21:34.390
Your Highness.

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:37.180
No, I know.

00:21:37.180 --> 00:21:38.370
A holiday, right?

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:41.050
I lost. There's nothing I can do.

00:21:41.050 --> 00:21:42.780
It's only for a short while, remember.

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:48.820
Yes, I'll take a short one.

00:21:54.220 --> 00:21:55.200
Huh?

00:21:56.230 --> 00:21:57.420
Seiran.

00:21:57.420 --> 00:21:59.540
You're too kind.

00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:03.150
No, I'm just afraid of losing him.

00:22:03.150 --> 00:22:05.050
I'll stay beside you.

00:22:05.860 --> 00:22:09.410
No matter what happens, we'll stay beside you.

00:22:09.410 --> 00:22:11.550
Oujo-sama and I will be here.

00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:18.390
By the way, if there are any left, may I take some of those dumplings home?

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:21.030
Ah? Take as many as you like.

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:25.150
Eighteen years old... think about it!

00:22:25.150 --> 00:22:26.450
She's in the prime of life!

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:28.470
And she's quite cute when you look at her closely.

00:22:28.470 --> 00:22:31.060
Just the thought of a girl being there makes you feel like working.

00:22:31.060 --> 00:22:34.490
Basically, that's the way men are.

00:22:34.490 --> 00:22:35.410
Tan-tan...

00:22:35.810 --> 00:22:41.040
If you keep measuring people by your own standards, I won't help you, no matter what happens.

00:22:41.040 --> 00:22:46.210
If you think all men are going to be kind and protect you, like your family retainer does,

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:47.720
then you're completely wrong.

00:22:47.720 --> 00:22:49.700
Y-Yes.

00:22:50.220 --> 00:22:55.730
Good. Anyway, they're quite harmless, and they've even said you're cute.

00:22:55.730 --> 00:22:59.230
If only she had bigger breasts...

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:05.130
Break's over!

00:23:05.130 --> 00:23:06.230
Let's do it!

00:23:07.840 --> 00:23:09.100
Line up!

00:23:09.100 --> 00:23:12.110
I'll ask each of you which department you want to go to.

00:23:19.650 --> 00:23:24.500
Whether you're fired and sent home, or get to stay in the Imperial Court, is up to you.

00:24:45.290 --> 00:24:48.330
Honestly! Everyone show your spirit, spirit!

00:24:48.330 --> 00:24:51.210
If you don't find a job soon, you'll be fired, fired!

00:24:51.480 --> 00:24:53.880
Run as fast as you can!

00:24:53.880 --> 00:24:55.910
No! The sun's setting again!
